What is code, what is content
-----------------------------

Code (MIT):
  * src/, ops/, tests/, rules/ (the semgrep ruleset), evals/ tooling,
    docker/, .github/, and the build configuration
  * the website's source: site/src/ components, layouts, styles and
    scripts, site/public/ scripts, and the code of every page and endpoint
  * the published scan data (site/src/data/, the JSON API at
    https://mcpwatchman.com/api/) — EXCEPT the excerpts it quotes from
    scanned servers' source, which remain their authors' and are quoted
    for analysis; no licence to them is granted here
  * README.md and the other repository documentation

Content (CC BY 4.0):
  * the prose of the website at https://mcpwatchman.com — the text of
    its pages (site/src/pages/), including the explanation of the
    methodology, and the prose of /llms.txt

Trademarks (NOT licensed):
  * the "mcpwatchman" name, and the mark drawn in
    site/src/components/Wordmark.astro and site/public/favicon.svg

